{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgtSd2U7ueCTZeGCNfUpW7","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Per-lane field playbooks: the GM's label GRAMMAR per field family.\n\nThe dominant failure on the binary and script lanes is not analysis, it is spelling the GM's synthetic\nlabel (e.g. `pe_cli`, `if_guard`, `.text$<sym>`) under coarse per-set feedback. `lib/knowledge.py` holds the\nconfirmed VALUES and `lib/vocab.json` the confirmed label lists; this module adds, per (lane, field-family):\nthe derivation RULE, the known-REJECTED spellings, and worked examples, and exposes them to the two consumers\nthat need them up front:\n\n  - for_lane(lane)                         -> markdown block injected into the worker prompts (point: start\n                                              from the rule, not blind synonyms)\n  - entry_for(lane, aid)                   -> the PlaybookEntry matching a field by its ending, or None\n  - rejected(lane, aid)                    -> spellings already proven wrong for this family (never reprobe)\n  - seed_candidates(lane, aid, terms, v)   -> high-priority label candidates for `hctf labels`, built from the\n                                              rule (closed vocab, or container+runtime / keyword+ending compounds)\n\nSingle source of truth for the confirmed values stays in lib/knowledge.py (imported below). Add a new family\nhere the moment the GM confirms one, next to the knowledge.py entry.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nfrom . import knowledge as K\n\nBINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\nSCRIPT = \"script-analysis\"\nMETADATA = \"metadata-forensics\"\n\n\ndef field_family(aid):\n    \"\"\"Group fields by their trailing token: 'batch-launcher-control'->'control', 'd03_analysis_format'->'format',\n    'set2.cpp-mangled_score_symbol'->'symbol'. Mirrors hctf.labels.ending so the resolver and playbook agree.\"\"\"\n    last = str(aid).rsplit(\".\", 1)[-1]\n    parts = [p for p in re.split(r\"[-_]\", last) if p]\n    return parts[-1].lower() if parts else last.lower()\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass PlaybookEntry:\n    lanes: tuple           # lanes this applies to\n    families: tuple        # field-family endings (field_family(aid)) it covers\n24:BINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\n25:SCRIPT = \"script-analysis\"\n26:METADATA = \"metadata-forensics\"\n29:def field_family(aid):\n49:def _symbol_derive(terms, solver_value):\n61:def _vbs_control_derive(terms, solver_value):\n74:def _hex_width_derive(terms, solver_value):\n85:PLAYBOOK = [\n248:def entries_for_lane(lane):\n252:def entry_for(lane, aid):\n260:def rejected(lane, aid):\n268:def seed_candidates(lane, aid, terms=(), solver_value=None):\n282:ENUM_NOTE = (\n293:NAMING_LAWS = (\n311:def for_lane(lane):\n# Day 9 \"Built Different\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-09 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets; 0 wrong):\n# pe.coff_machine_u16_hex is IMAGE_FILE_HEADER.Machine (u16 LE at e_lfanew+4, after 'PE\\0\\0') as \"0x\" + 4 zero-padded\n# LOWERCASE hex digits: Go 386 PE32 -> \"0x014c\". NOT the binary lane's word (\"i386\", PE_MACHINE) -- a `_u16_hex` suffix\n# asks for the raw constant. Unpadded \"0x14c\" never tried; only i386 seen (every \"several architectures\" decoy was i386).\nPE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT = \"0x{:04x}\"\n\n# Day 10 \"Where Do We Begin?\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-12 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets): id\n# d09-pe-NNN-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex = OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint (u32 LE at e_lfanew+24+16, the raw\n# RVA -- not ImageBase+RVA) as \"0x\" + 8 zero-padded lowercase hex digits, e.g. \"0x00065bd0\". The id names no width:\n# pad to the STRUCT field's size (u32 -> 8), same law as the D9 u16. Unpadded \"0x65bd0\" REJECTED (D10 single).\n# Rehearsal D10 (TT d5b62c7e, Mastery 1f84320c): PE32+ x86-64/AArch64 too (\"0x00063a80\", \"0x00063510\") -- the width is the\n# FIELD's (u32), not the PE32/PE32+ flavour, while answer_format only says \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x prefix\".\nPE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT = \"0x{:08x}\"\nPE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_REJECTED = [\"0x65bd0\"]\n\n# MITRE ATT&CK technique the GM expects per scripting scenario (script-analysis), confirmed Day 1 \"Power Play\".","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b91bdd74-729a-4aee-94d0-8b48c90d173c","uuid":"55233fdc-94ce-498e-b024-a3801b4bb8b1","timestamp":"2026-10-12T01:58:29.280Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Per-lane field playbooks: the GM's label GRAMMAR per field family.\n\nThe dominant failure on the binary and script lanes is not analysis, it is spelling the GM's synthetic\nlabel (e.g. `pe_cli`, `if_guard`, `.text$<sym>`) under coarse per-set feedback. `lib/knowledge.py` holds the\nconfirmed VALUES and `lib/vocab.json` the confirmed label lists; this module adds, per (lane, field-family):\nthe derivation RULE, the known-REJECTED spellings, and worked examples, and exposes them to the two consumers\nthat need them up front:\n\n  - for_lane(lane)                         -> markdown block injected into the worker prompts (point: start\n                                              from the rule, not blind synonyms)\n  - entry_for(lane, aid)                   -> the PlaybookEntry matching a field by its ending, or None\n  - rejected(lane, aid)                    -> spellings already proven wrong for this family (never reprobe)\n  - seed_candidates(lane, aid, terms, v)   -> high-priority label candidates for `hctf labels`, built from the\n                                              rule (closed vocab, or container+runtime / keyword+ending compounds)\n\nSingle source of truth for the confirmed values stays in lib/knowledge.py (imported below). Add a new family\nhere the moment the GM confirms one, next to the knowledge.py entry.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nfrom . import knowledge as K\n\nBINARY = \"binary-reverse-engineering\"\nSCRIPT = \"script-analysis\"\nMETADATA 