ed Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider,","-  JavaScript-interface origin trust, cleartext session transport, permissive X509 trust manager). The theme was","+  JavaScript-interface origin trust, cleartext session transport, permissive X509 trust manager, Network Security Config","+  exception, locally stored credential in SharedPreferences). The theme was","   flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even when the dex carried a matching stub class (d7 `WebViewBridge`,","   d8 `CleartextSession`, d9 `TrustEveryone`) or the prompt demanded a live action (\"replay it against the backend\"","   d8, \"exploit a challenge CA\" d9 -- no CA/cert/network_security_config/TrustManager code was shipped)."," - What actually varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split,","-  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery","+  hex, caesar+key, reverse again on d8, base64 again on d9, split again on d10, xor+key again on d11 -- codecs CAN repeat). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery","   sets) used the same codec. Keys re-roll per variant. A new codec name is possible any day: decode it from the first","   4 chars, which must become `ANS-`. The dex also holds the codec name as a `CODEC` string constant (d8, d9) and a","   `DAY-NN:<theme_id>:<mechanic>` string."]},{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":14,"newStart":25,"newLines":14,"lines":["   routine. `lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain for that case."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)","-- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but `key` (xor byte d4, caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4) and any","+- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but `key` (xor byte d4, d11: 81/109/205; caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4) and any","   split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time. Keyless codecs","   (d8 `reverse`, d9 `base64`, 7 variants each) differed only in `data`. Rule: decode by declared codec, regex-check, else `decode_any`."," - **Per-variant identity** -- case ref, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback attempt slug","   change per variant (all Mastery sets shared one slug on d7-d9, e.g. `d09-92be5cd6e8a5594f`; single and TT each","   had their own). APK size stays 12704 B, 6 entries. None of these feed the answer."," - **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>.apk` per set, often identically named: pair by sha256. Set count","-  varies: 3 sets (d1-d7), 5 sets on d8 and d9 (`set1..set5.answer`). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3.","+  varies: 3 sets (d1-d7, d10-d11), 5 sets on d8 and d9 (`set1..set5.answer`). Loop over the contract's answer_ids, never assume 3."," - **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON; if it decodes to nothing, fall back to dex/resources","   (`lib.android.extract_answer` chain) rather than assuming the sample's location."," "]},{"oldStart":131,"oldLines":12,"newStart":133,"newLines":28,"lines":[" - Start 13:00:07Z -> CORRECT 13:00:32.6Z = 25s, first try. TT (8s window) correct in 3.16s (solve phase 1.99s --","   cold imports; keep top-level imports light). Mastery (11s window, 5 sets) correct in 1.7s. Zero wrong submissions."," ","+**Day 10 — Network Config Split** (mechanic \"Network Security Config exception\"): first fixture with extra entries --","+`res/xml/network_security_config.xml` (cleartextTrafficPermitted=true for domain 127.0.0.1) + `resources.arsc`. Still","+static: codec `split` (repeat of d5), `parts [\"56C4B5B0D\",\"ANS-4\",\"9D8953\"]`, `order [2,0,1]` = output slot of each part.","+All 3 modes CORRECT first try (TT 13 s / Mastery 10 s windows, 3 sets).","+","+**Day 11 — Local Secrets** (mechanic `DAY-11:shared_preferences:locally stored synthetic credential`; prompt \"Separate","+active credentials from decoys across generated local stores.\")","+- Same 6-entry fixture (12704 B). No SharedPreferences XML, sqlite or other \"local store\" file shipped; the only","+  credential-looking string besides the asset is the dex's loopback `client_secret=SECRET-<22 hex>` (a decoy, never","+  the answer). Codec `xor` (repeat of d4): `{\"data\":\"EB8CfGkXY2NkZmVmYBUXZWkVYGU=\",\"key\":81}` -> b64-decode, XOR 81 ->","+  `ANS-8F2257471DF48D14`.","+- Worker (warm launch): one command decoded the triage-extracted JSON by hand (`base64 -d | xor 81`), a second filled","+  `answer()` with `lib.android.puzzle_candidates` + `ANS-` regex (fallback `raw_entry_scan`/`dex_strings`) and","+  submitted. Launch 01:55:40Z -> CORRECT 01:56:08Z = ~28 s, first try. TT (7 s window) 0.93 s in-window; Mastery (8 s, 3","+  sets, keys 205/...) 0.82 s. Zero wrong submissions.","+"," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3 sets d1-d7, 5 on d8-d9), one","   APK per set."," - Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding and add no","   whitespace.","-- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-9). `ANS-<16 uppercase hex>` confirmed","+- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-11). `ANS-<16 uppercase hex>` confirmed","   again on d8 and d9 (7/7 variants each). The GM accepts the decoded","   `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"invoke ... return the backend","   evidence code\"."]},{"oldStart":161,"oldLines":7,"newStart":179,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Don't decompile when you don't need to.** Every solve so far (d1-d9) needed only the asset; the manifest was context only.","   Keep jadx/apktool for the day the asset is missing or lacks `ANS-`."," - **Prompt wording escalates, 