{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwXGpmsNW5zu6Ba6FtxV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Day 11 went 15/15 CORRECT on the first try. The single solves took about 25–55 s from launch, and the timed modes finished in 0.8–4.9 s inside their windows. The required tests and `lib.refs.coverage 11` all pass, and I didn't commit anything.\n\n1. **Logs:** I added a Day 11 entry to all five technique logs and updated their summary, recognition-cue, pitfall and variant-axis sections. Day 11 was:\n   - **Warmups:** the blob was URL-safe base64 with the `=` padding dropped.\n   - **Metadata:** the answer was the PE version resource's `OriginalFilename`, which changed with the build's architecture (386, amd64, arm64).\n   - **Mobile:** the answer came from the usual puzzle asset again, using the xor codec.\n   - **Binary:** the new member was a program written in the D language. No new field was asked; the config offset rule from Day 9 held.\n   - **Scripting:** four TypeScript files and two new Bash advanced-syntax files.\n\n   The warmups, mobile and script-analysis logs had no Day 10 entry, so I added short ones from the stored bytes. I also shortened older entries to keep each log near 200 lines; script-analysis is still 237.\n2. **Merged into lib:** `lib.decode.decode_chunk` now decodes URL-safe base64 with the padding removed. The warmups worker had to write this by hand. With the change, `decode_chunked` alone gets all 53 confirmed Mastery answers; before, line 11 came out as garbage. I added a check in `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`, and all 63 stored warmups cases from Days 1–11 still pass.\n3. **Also merged:** confirmed facts in `lib/knowledge.py`:\n   - the PE version-string rule for metadata;\n   - the config-offset rule re-confirmed on the D build;\n   - the TypeScript role-to-ATT&CK table;\n   - the two new Bash feature/primitive pairs.\n4. **Rejected:** `fast_aes_unzip` (proposed in the binary notes) is solver code, and the rules say solver code doesn't go into lib. `iter_entries(leaf_ext=...)` is already in `lib/common.py` from the Day 9 ratchet.\n5. **Rejected:** `gm_error_body` and the download retry on `rate_limited` belong in `hctf/`, which I'm not allowed to touch. Both proposals were also carried over from older solver notes, not written today."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":660,"cache_read_input_tokens":181977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":660},"output_tokens":785,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b91bdd74-729a-4aee-94d0-8b48c90d173c","uuid":"b4d0e502-95bd-4135-ba36-c046586c7bff","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:04:41.438Z","request_id":"req_011CfwXGorJFsk4NGNwJxmj2"}
